{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpCkWdK8gUpj2JHQkzNnZY","type":"tool_result","content":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #406\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/config/types.go`, `raw.go`, `defaults.go`, `render.go`: add `Approvals` to `Intervals` (new, default 1m via new `defaultIntervalApprovals`), `approvals` to `rawIntervals.parse` (both the `set(...)` call and the accepted-key switch and its \"unknown key\" message), `intervalOr` in the resolve step and the minimum-1m check list (`intervals.approvals`), and `intervalsYAML`/`Intervals` rendering. Reason: the schema rejects unknown keys, so the key must exist before use.\n2. `internal/controller/controller.go`: add exported `func (c *Controller) WakeLoops(reason string, names ...string)`. It sends non-blocking on each named runner's existing `r.wake` channel (capacity 1, so pending wakes merge; a loop mid-tick runs once more, as for #394), ignores unknown names and calls after shutdown, and logs `controller.wake` with `reason` and the loops actually woken. Keep the runners reachable from the Controller (store them in a field set in `Run`, guarded by `c.mu`). Add a short debounce reusing the `wakeOnFreed` pattern (`FreedDebounce`/`DefaultFreedDebounce`): collect the names requested within the window into a set, then wake once per loop. Paused handling stays in `runner` tick code, so a wake while paused does nothing; check that path in `scheduler.go` and do not add a bypass.\n3. `internal/controller` (new `approvals.go`): `ApprovalWatch` loop-like goroutine started from `Run`. Deps: a `Search func(ctx, q string) ([]github.Issue, error)` (from `github.Reader.SearchIssues`), clock, interval, `DryRun`-agnostic since it only reads. Each interval run searches, in one or a few queries: `is:open label:ard:approved -label:ard:worker:*` (use the prefix exclusion as the label catalogue allows; otherwise filter in Go by `labels` package), plus open items carrying a triage-done label, and items that lost `ard:needs-human` or `ard:executor:failed`. Removal cannot be searched directly, so for the unblock case find items with `ard:triage:*:done`/worker/review `request` or `done` state and no `needs-human`/`executor:failed`, and keep an in-memory \"seen with needs-human or executor:failed\" set; a later absence wakes the owning loop (`reason=unblocked`). Worker must confirm exact queries against `internal/labels` and what `triage/loop.go`, `workers` and `reviewer/loop.go` already search for. A hit on approval wakes `triage` (`reason=approval`); an unblocked item wakes the loop that owns its stage label. Skip when the kill switch is on (use the same `Pauser` as ticks) and do nothing but read in dry-run. Errors are logged and retried next interval; no agent, no slot.\n4. `internal/servecmd/serve.go`: wire the watch into `controller.Deps` (new field e.g. `Approvals *ApprovalWatchDeps`) with `d.Reader.SearchIssues` and `cfg.Intervals.Approvals` read from the fresh config each run; register `approvals` in `knownLoops` only if it should be selectable with `--loops`, otherwise leave it implicit. Give `controller.Controller` to the closer via a late-bound hook (the Controller is built after the closer), e.g. a `wiring.wake atomic.Pointer[func(reason string, names ...string)]` set after `controller.New`.\n5. `internal/closeout/closeout.go`: add `Deps.Wake func(reason string, names ...string)` (optional, nil skips). In `advance`, after `c.finish` succeeds (and before or after `PhaseClosed` is saved; do it once, also on resume paths; a double wake is harmless) compute loops from `rec.Plan`: `Requests` and `Terminal` with `ard:worker:*` → `workers`; `ard:review:*` → `reviewers`; `ard:triage:*` or `ard:pending` → `triage`; a PR marked ready (find the effect in `postReview`/`review.go`) → `merger`; a review round request (changes requested, see `ReviewChanged`) → `workers` (and `reviewfix` if that loop owns it). Add pure helper `func WakeTargets(p Plan, j Job) []string` (new) so it is unit-testable. Skip on dry-run and on failed/retry outcomes. Reason `closeout`.\n6. `internal/servecmd/reaping.go`: pass `Wake` in `closeout.New(closeout.Deps{...})`, delegating to the late-bound controller hook from step 4.\n7. `docs/proposal.md`: update the triage gate, worker and reviewer loop sections, \"One pool of job slots\" (line ~310) and the Configuration intervals table (new `intervals.approvals`, default 1m, minimum 1m): hand-offs wake the next loop, approvals are polled by the watch, the gate still does the real check. Also update the comment about intervals in config docs if any (`ard config check` text).\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `make lint test`. All with fake clock and the GitHub fake; no network.\n- `internal/config/load_test.go`: `intervals.approvals` unset → 1m; `30s` → error naming `intervals.approvals`; `2m` accepted; unknown-key message lists approvals; render round trip.\n- `internal/closeout` (new `wake_test.go`): `WakeTargets` per outcome: worker requested → `[workers]`; review requested → `[reviewers]`; lead requests triage roles → `[triage]`; `ard:pending` → `[triage]`; review passed, PR ready → `[merger]`; review changes requested → `[workers]`; failed/retry/needs-human only → none; dry-run → Wake not called; Wake not called when a label effect fails; Wake called once on resume.\n- `internal/controller/wake_test.go` (new, patterned on `freed_test.go`): WakeLoops wakes only named loops; burst of 10 calls inside the debounce gives one tick per loop; call during a running tick gives exactly one extra tick; unknown name ignored; paused controller runs nothing; log has `reason` and loops.\n- `internal/controller/approvals_test.go` (new): a fake search hit wakes triage with `reason=approval`; no hit no wake; needs-human or executor:failed removal wakes the owning loop (`unblocked`); paused → no search effects/wake; dry-run → read only, no writes; search error is logged and next run proceeds.\n- `internal/triage` existing gate tests: add a case that an approval from the wrong actor or before triage finished still starts no worker even after a watch wake (gate unchanged; assert in `fanin` tests).\n- Integration in `internal/servecmd`: worker close-out opening a PR with `ard:review:<role>` wakes reviewers; engineer close-out with `require_approval: false` wakes workers.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. Controller scheduling and close-out are core code with concurrency (wake channels, debounce goroutine, late-bound hook between Closer and Controller). Wakes only trigger ticks that are still gated by the kill switch, the pool and the approval gate, so authorisation does not change. Adds GitHub search reads once a minute (rate limits). No migrations. No path in `merge.protected_paths` is touched; the stopgap interval change in `.ard/config.yaml` is a separate human PR.\n\n### Size\nL, about 700–1000 changed lines including tests. Files: `internal/config/{types,raw,defaults,render,load_test}.go`, `internal/controller/{controller.go,approvals.go,wake_test.go,approvals_test.go}`, `internal/closeout/{closeout.go,wake.go,wake_test.go}`, `internal/servecmd/{serve.go,reaping.go}` and tests, `docs/proposal.md`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fa3a14c-7971-4f48-b6d5-38e23cfe8596","uuid":"7f7b18b8-8120-4925-bb48-8c77e3dba48c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:35:01.057Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #406\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/config/types.go`, `raw.go`, `defaults.go`, `render.go`: add `Approvals` to `Intervals` (new, default 1m via new `defaultIntervalApprovals`), `approvals` to `rawIntervals.parse` (both the `set(...)` call and the accepted-key switch and its \"unknown key\" message), `intervalOr` in the resolve step and the minimum-1m check list (`intervals.approvals`), and `intervalsYAML`/`Intervals` r